The HTML another program puts on the Wayland clipboard beside its text (`text/html`), read with the text and kept
as the item's metadata, `{"text/html": "<html>"}`, so the app's rich-text editor pastes what it can of its formats
(through teams-proto's sanitizing reader). A UTF-16 one (with its byte order mark) is decoded. Our own
copies keep their item as they were (the self-offer path is untouched).

diff -ruN a/src/linux/wayland/clipboard.rs b/src/linux/wayland/clipboard.rs
--- a/src/linux/wayland/clipboard.rs
+++ b/src/linux/wayland/clipboard.rs
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@
 /// Text mime types that we'll accept from other programs.
 pub(crate) const ALLOWED_TEXT_MIME_TYPES: [&str; 2] = ["text/plain;charset=utf-8", "UTF8_STRING"];
 
+/// ngteams: the HTML a rich-text paste reads beside the text.
+const HTML_MIME_TYPE: &str = "text/html";
+
 pub(crate) struct Clipboard {
     connection: Connection,
     loop_handle: LoopHandle<'static, ()>,
@@ -114,9 +117,42 @@
         // copying from eg: firefox inserts a lot of blank
